  "expectedDraftMasterHash": "sha256:14e0dc724013feeafe0c9be9466c81569c8d893467bac46653452acb9359e351",
  "visualBrief": "Main Belo Monte dam at the retained exact map identity. Both rock-fill arms, intake headwall, eighteen exposed penstocks, the full native green-roof powerhouse including the west wing, river-facing transformer apron, outfall arcade and the mapped tailrace divider.",
  "heightPolicy": "The reservoir datum comes from the standard Terrarium sample at local [0,620]. The layout uses the exact retained dam polygon and the single current PMTiles powerhouse footprint. Elevations, pipe diameters and grades are picture and standard-terrain estimates. The supplier confirms eighteen main units, and the aerial identifies the exposed penstock arrangement. The separately located Pimental site and diversion corridor are outside this main-dam reconstruction.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X nearly east along the main powerhouse, +Z south into the intermediate reservoir, -Z north downstream to the Xingu. +Y up.",
