      "observed": "Main Belo Monte dam at the retained exact map identity. Both rock-fill arms, intake headwall, eighteen exposed penstocks, the full native green-roof powerhouse including the west wing, river-facing transformer apron, outfall arcade and the mapped tailrace divider. The reservoir datum comes from the standard Terrarium sample at local [0,620]. The layout uses the exact retained dam polygon and the single current PMTiles powerhouse footprint. Elevations, pipe diameters and grades are picture and standard-terrain estimates. The supplier confirms eighteen main units, and the aerial identifies the exposed penstock arrangement. The separately located Pimental site and diversion corridor are outside this main-dam reconstruction."
